From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vipul Cariappa <vipulcariappa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:26:23 +0530
Subject: Track the preloaded python files as link dependencies

--preload-file arguments are opaque to CMake, and the earlier fix for this named
only libcppjit.so. Editing cppjit's python layer therefore relinked nothing:
xcpp.data kept the previous copy and the kernel went on running code that no
longer existed in the source tree.

That is worse than a stale build, because the failure mode is indistinguishable
from a fix that does not work. Two changes were tested and dismissed here before
a grep through xcpp.data showed the old text still in it. Name the files that
actually change during development so the relink happens.

(cherry picked from commit 9b8ed5f710120220847d370e81b103cc97076563)
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 81446e1..87371d8 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -525,8 +525,16 @@ if(EMSCRIPTEN)
     # on its own leaves xcpp.data holding the previous copy and the kernel
     # silently keeps running the old code. Name the ones that get rebuilt during
     # development as link dependencies so the relink happens.
+    # Directories preloaded above are opaque to CMake as well, so name the files
+    # that actually change during development. Without these, editing cppjit's
+    # python layer relinks nothing, xcpp.data keeps the previous copy, and the
+    # kernel runs code that no longer exists in the source tree -- a fix can
+    # then appear not to work when it was simply never deployed.
     set_property(TARGET xcpp APPEND PROPERTY LINK_DEPENDS
-        "${CPPJIT_BUILD_DIR}/libcppjit.so")
+        "${CPPJIT_BUILD_DIR}/libcppjit.so"
+        "${CPPJIT_SOURCE_DIR}/python/cppjit/__init__.py"
+        "${CPPJIT_SOURCE_DIR}/python/cppjit/_cpython_cppjit.py"
+        "${CPPJIT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/cpyrt/API.h")
 endif()
 # Tests
 # =====
